KZ3 patch 2093: device-resident vertex cache fill without UPLOAD-heap reads, and its profiler (LD_VTX_DEV_PROF=1); pass 88.

Patch 2092's fill built the draw's topology indices in the index ring (an UPLOAD-heap mapping, write-combined) and
then copied them ring -> staging block: a read of write-combined memory, 4.81 ms/frame for 2.5 MB of fills on K4
(r88-p1), most of the +3.8 ms that 2092 added to the walker's vertex copy bucket. The indices are now built in a CPU
scratch (rsx_vd_scratch) and copied to the ring and to the staging block from there (rsx_vd_stage_write), so both
UPLOAD mappings are only written: fill-stage 4.81 -> 0.08 ms/frame, copy bucket 6.81 -> 2.22 ms/frame (r88-p2). The
ring gets its indices before any early return of the fill, as before. Output bytes unchanged.

LD_VTX_DEV_PROF=1 (diagnostic, default off): QPC timers around the parts of the cache path (key, evict, valid,
ring, spans, fill-idx, fill-alloc, fill-malloc, fill-src, fill-stage, fill-queue, fill-drop, idx) in
`[vtx-dev-prof]` (cumulative ms) and a new-key classification in `[vtx-dev-keys]` (moved = same vertex stream and
same index bytes under another index offset; new-idx = same stream, new index bytes; reentry = a key seen before;
fresh = new stream), both printed with `[vtx-dev]` every 256 frames.

Host test: tools/smoke/test_vtx_dev.sh (adds the scratch growth and the staging layout: payload | pad | indices,
ring and staging indices equal, nothing written outside).

